Apply factory image via d-link http web-gui, or via recovery web interface.


===== Recovery / back to stock =====

  - Push and hold the reset button and turn on the power. Wait until all LEDs start rapidly blinking (~10sec.)
  - DHCP should give you an IP in the 192.168.123.0/24 subnet, or set one manually
  - Upload original factory image via JBOOT http interface at ''%%http://192.168.123.254/%%''
  - If http doesn't work, it can be done with curl command: ''%%curl -F FN=@XXXXX.bin http://192.168.123.254/upg%%'' where ''XXXXX.bin'' is the name of the firmware file.
  - You can optionally telnet to 192.168.123.254 before or during the upload and it will report the flashing status, memory address etc.
  - Once the flashing starts, the LEDs will start flashing a lot more slowly.
  - Once the flashing has completed, the LEDs will change the way they flash again, staying on mostly, with a brief flash off.
  - Once web UI and/or telnet says "Success", power cycle the router, or type "reboot" into the telnet session.

